note Translated from go src/time/format.go, parseSignedOffset.
note parse_signed_offset gives back the length of a signed hour offset such as "+07" at the start of value, or 0 if there is none.

note Go's leadingInt returns three values (x, rem, err); the number and the rest are returned as one record and the error as a failure.
type LeadingInt
    field number as a Nat
    field rem as Text

to leading_int text
    given text is Text
    produces a LeadingInt
    fails with LeadingIntOverflow

note WORKAROUND: the doc has no way to slice text (Go's value[1:]) or take its first byte (value[0]). These two helpers are declared so the body needs no invented syntax.
to text_until position of text
    given position is a Nat
    given text is Text
    produces Text

to text_after position of text
    given position is a Nat
    given text is Text
    produces Text

to parse_signed_offset value
    given value is Text
    produces an Int

    note UNCLEAR: Go panics if value is empty (value[0] is out of range). The original states no precondition, so none is added, and the doc does not say what text_until does past the end.
    note WORKAROUND: no character literals, so the sign is compared as a one-character Text
    let sign be text_until 1 of value
    if sign is not "-" and sign is not "+"
        give back 0
    let rest be text_after 1 of value
    note UNCLEAR: the doc never shows code after a handle block, so the rest of the operation sits inside it
    handle
        let parsed be try leading_int rest
        let x be number of parsed
        let remainder be rem of parsed
        note fail if nothing consumed by leadingInt
        if remainder is rest
            give back 0
        if x is more than 23
            give back 0
        give back count of value - count of remainder
    on failure LeadingIntOverflow
        give back 0
